    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_one_antipodal_primary_torsion_reducer",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 one-antipodal stratum has a sign-free primary/torsion circuit",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "If an official c=2 denominator contains one antipodal pair, common scaling gives roots {1,-1,c,d}. With S=c+d, P=cd, and X=S^2, the two primary coefficients are F_H(X,P) and S G_H(X,P). On the exactly-one-antipodal stratum they vanish exactly when F_H=G_H=0. Complementary-root torsion is the sign-free 39-step circuit U_0=X-2P, V_0=P^2, U_(j+1)=U_j^2-2V_j, V_(j+1)=V_j^2, ending at (2,1). Together with square and distinctness gates this is an exact two-variable circuit modulo S->-S. It does not prove the circuit empty, use the secondary gap, or prove C2-PAR.",
